id: pm-h6b73t
title: "The outcome-milestone ladder is a sibling set rather than a layer: 1,024 terminal items reach the roadmap apex through 154 typed roots without traversing any outcome milestone"
description: "Typed-reachability measurement over all 2,357 items shows the six outcome milestones sit beside the capability epics under the roadmap apex instead of between them, so 51 percent of the terminal record has no typed path through any outcome and shortest-path traversal can bypass the ladder even where an implements edge exists."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:graph",graph-governance,measurement,reachability,typed-edges
created_at: "2026-08-07T11:15:54.109Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-24T14:39:15.172Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-24T14:23:50.888Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-24T14:23:50.888Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "Depth-to-outcome is measured and reported for every item in the workspace, not only active ones, and the report distinguishes reaching the index root from reaching an outcome; The apex-versus-ladder topology is dispositioned explicitly: either outcome milestones become an intermediate layer that capability epics resolve through, or the invariant is restated to name the apex as the target and the ladder as advisory; Every one of the 154 typed roots either gains an evidence-cited edge that places it on an outcome path, or appears on a recorded residual list naming why no durable evidence supports one; No edge is added to satisfy a count; each added edge cites the durable text, history event, or linked artifact it was derived from; A regression that reintroduces a ladder-bypassing root fails the graph audit rather than being discovered by a later measurement pass"
goal: project management = context management
objective: "Every item, terminal or active, resolves to an outcome through a typed and explainable path"
value: "Graph algorithms can answer which outcome any recorded work served, across the project's whole timeline rather than only its forward backlog"
why_now: The outcome ladder has existed since 2026-07-25 and the terminal backfill waves are about to run; aiming them without this measurement repeats the active-only scoping mistake
parent: pm-96h7
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
resolution: "Reconstructed the portfolio hierarchy through evidence-cited implements and supersedes edges, measured all-status depth-to-outcome, retained only justified historical exceptions, and ratcheted outcome reachability in the tracker-context-quality assurance gate."
expected_result: "A typed traversal from any item, closed or open, reaches an outcome milestone, and the outcome milestone lies on the path rather than beside it"
actual_result: "Current all-status graph audit over 2,538 nodes reports 289 active and 2,240 terminal outcome-reachable nodes, zero active or terminal outcome-unreachable nodes, 10000 basis points of reachability, no active hierarchy violation, and only seven preserved terminal legacy hierarchy divergences outside this issue's scope."
