comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T12:16:57.594Z","harness:claude-code","text=Ladder topology resolved 2026-08-10 by measurement rather than by argument, and the acceptance criteria are now largely met.\n\nMethod: build the up-graph over hierarchy-bearing kinds only (implements, parent, child_of, plus the parent scalar), then ask of every item in the workspace — terminal included — whether it reaches any of the six outcome milestones, whether it reaches only the apex, or neither. Active-scoped checks cannot see this question, which is why the topology survived so long.\n\nBaseline before the pass: 15 of 89 epics reached an outcome milestone; 2,225 items reached an outcome; 37 reached the apex with no outcome; 143 reached neither; 130 items had no hierarchy up-edge at all.\n\nThree evidence-cited waves followed, all edges derived from each item's own recorded title, description, or tag vocabulary — never to satisfy a count.\n\n1. Strategic layer. 63 implements edges wiring every capability epic and every v1 delivery-epoch epic to the outcome milestone its own domain names, plus 8 supersedes edges joining the canonical v1 milestones to their archived PRD-numbered duplicates and one era-succession join.\n2. Parentless-terminal lineage. 118 implements edges routing every terminal item with no up-edge to the capability epic its title names. Classification was rule-based on the title with discovery-channel tags stripped first, because a defect found via telemetry is not a telemetry defect; 23 assignments were then corrected by review where a keyword named the channel or a homonym rather than the subject.\n3. Apex bypass. 31 implements edges giving the review-pass containers and recent PR-cycle findings parented straight to the apex an outcome path through the capability layer.\n\nResult: apex-bypassing items 37 to 0. Items reaching no outcome 143 to 11, and those 11 are the recorded residual, not a remainder — 8 canceled PRD duplicate encodings reachable from their canonical sibling via supersedes, and 3 canceled invalid sub-agent probe artifacts with no programme lineage to claim. Rootless items 130 to 12. Items at ancestry depth 4 or deeper rose from 460 to 1,036.\n\nThe disposition this item asked for is therefore settled in favour of the first branch: outcome milestones are an intermediate layer that capability epics resolve through, not advisory siblings. The regression guard is in place as of the same day — the implements floor moved 2305 to 2544 with a note naming this wave, so deleting the layer now fails the tracker measurement ratchet instead of being found by a later pass."
  "2026-08-24T14:23:50.013Z","harness:codex","Closure evidence 2026-08-24: direct pm graph audit --full examined all 2,538 nodes and 12,504 deduplicated directed edges; active outcome reachability is 289/289 and terminal outcome reachability is 2,240/2,240, with zero outcome-unreachable nodes. pnpm quality:tracker-measurements passed all 41 assertions, including graph outcome reachability at 10,000 basis points with a blocking zero-unreachable ceiling and proven negative controls. The prior comment records the evidence-cited topology waves and explicit ladder disposition; no density-only edge was added in this closure."
